          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>What is the primary factor responsible for the rising global incidence of multiple pregnancies?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Increasing maternal age at conception</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>While advanced maternal age is associated with a higher natural rate of dizygotic twinning, the video identifies ART — ovulation induction and IVF — as the primary driver of the global rise.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Widespread use of assisted reproductive technology</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>ART, including ovulation induction with clomiphene (6–8% twin rate) and IVF with multiple embryo transfer (historically 25–30% twin rate), is the primary driver of the rising incidence of multiple pregnancies.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Improved ultrasonographic detection of twin pregnancies</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Better detection identifies more twins at earlier gestational ages but does not increase the true incidence. The rise is due to ART actually increasing the occurrence of multiple conceptions.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Increased dietary folate supplementation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Folate supplementation is recommended periconceptionally but has no established link to multifollicular development or increased twinning rates. The primary driver is ART.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The primary driver is assisted reproductive technology. Clomiphene carries a 6–8% twin rate, and IVF with double embryo transfer historically resulted in a 25–30% twin rate."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! ART — both ovulation induction and IVF with multiple embryo transfer — is the primary driver of the global rise in multiple pregnancies."
                }
              ],
